+## Built State (2026-09-21, at the close)
+What F277 has on disk at its close, so a later reader need not reconstruct it from the
+ledger. F277 reached the standing seven-session soft limit at its round 11 of 25 and closes
+at a split scope by DECISION F277 D10; what moved is named at the end of this section.
+
+**T001 — COMPLETE.** `packages/orchestration/event_names.py` is dependency-free and declares
+84 names in `EVENT_NAMES` and 2 in `RETIRED_EVENT_NAMES`, with `is_declared_event`,
+`assert_declared_event` and `known_event_names` over them.
+`tests/orchestration/test_event_names.py` collects WRITTEN names and READ names from the AST
+of `packages/` and `apps/` and asserts both are subsets of `EVENT_NAMES | RETIRED_EVENT_NAMES`;
+a reader for a name neither set holds reddens it, red-proved. Every `RETIRED_EVENT_NAMES`
+entry cites the dated ruling that retired it and names a module that still reads it, both
+asserted from the source. The collector found SIX names read and never written rather than
+the two the "Why this exists" section counted, and DECISION F277 D5 disposed of all six:
+`worker_adapters_listed` and the readiness half of `patch_intent_reverted` deleted with what
+they fed, `approval_decision` repointed at the names the repository writes,
+`command_discovery_completed` given the writer its readers had always named, and
+`patch_intent_reverted` and `stop_reason_recorded` recorded as retirements rather than
+accidents. The readiness dimension that had scored absent since the day it was written is
+therefore gone rather than silently wrong, which is the disposition the slice required.
+
+**T002 — COMPLETE.** `apps/cli/json_envelope.py` carries one shape — `schema_version`, `ok`,
+and for a failure `error` and `message` — behind `build_ok`, `build_error`, `emit_ok`,
+`emit_error` and `fail`, serialised with `sort_keys=True`, with the envelope's two reserved
+keys refused to a payload at the call site rather than silently overwritten.
+`apps/cli/grouped.py` wraps dispatch in a catch-all boundary that routes through `emit_error`
+under `--json` and through a one-line stderr message otherwise and exits 1; `SystemExit` and
+`KeyboardInterrupt` pass through untouched, the first because it is how every handler in this
+CLI ends deliberately and the second because swallowing it would make Ctrl-C look like a
+crash. DECISION F277 D6 records why the boundary catches `Exception` and not a project
+exception base: there is no such base, and the failures that actually reached an operator as
+a traceback were the undeclared ones. `tests/cli/test_json_envelope.py` pins the shape and
+the boundary, red-proved by a handler that raises.
+
+**T003 — APPLIED IN PART; THE REMAINDER IS F283's T001.** The helper
+`fail(error, message, *, json_output, exit_code=1, **payload)` exists, returns `NoReturn`, and
+is the spelling DECISION F277 D7 fixed — `error` and `exit_code`, never `code`. Nine command
+modules call it and hold no `sys.exit` of their own: `blocker.py`, `change.py`,
+`contract_cmd.py`, `event.py`, `file.py`, `job_context_cmd.py`, `memory.py`, `mission_cmd.py`
+and `worker.py`, migrated one group per commit across rounds 6 to 11, each with its own
+mutation red-proofs. Twenty-one files under `apps/cli/` still hold a `sys.exit` call, 203 of
+them in total excluding the helper's own two. DECISION F277 D8 (a token is named for the
+CONDITION, so the same condition reads the same in every group) and DECISION F277 D9 (a
+catch-all exception gets a catch-all token named for the layer that refused) are the token
+rules those nine groups were migrated under, and they bind the remaining nineteen unchanged.
+NOT DONE here: the catalog half — the read-only commands that do not declare `supports_json`,
+33 of them when D7 measured the set at `62b40261` — and the two false declarations D7's part
+(d) found, `init run` and `dev status`, which each honour a `--json` argument while the
+catalog says they cannot.
+
+**T004 — NOT STARTED; IT IS F283's T002, WHOLE.** No exit code has a documented meaning yet
+and `tests/cli/test_json_contract.py` does not exist. The sweep is the acceptance evidence for
+T003 as well as for itself, which is why it moves with the slice it measures rather than being
+attempted over a half-migrated surface.
+
+**WHAT MOVED TO F283** (`docs/roadmap/features/T2_F283.md`, registered in the same commit that
+struck them from the Acceptance list above): T003's remainder — the nineteen unmigrated
+modules, `runtime_cmd.py` among them as its own round, and the catalog half — as F283's T001;
+T004 whole as F283's T002; three Acceptance bullets verbatim; and finding R-1014, for whatever
+half of its fix clause this closure's own checklist consolidation does not land. DECISIONs
+F277 D5 through D9 stay here, because they are rulings about what was built, and F283's file
+names the three that bind its own work.
